  "drySha": "5e6caaa7c0706db3ab8d17f5c4643100e08b4438",
  "author": "groundnuty <groundnuty@gmail.com>",
  "date": "2026-08-06T20:13:36Z",
  "subject": "fix: hydrator helm.namespace -- destination.namespace alone doesn't reach helm template",
  "body": "Live finding, Task 4 clean-room: the Application CRD documents\nsourceHydrator.drySource.helm.namespace as defaulting to the app's\ndestination.namespace when left empty -- but on this ArgoCD version\n(chart 10.1.3, appVersion v3.5.0-rc2, the Source Hydrator's beta/rc\nchannel per environments/kind/argocd-values.yaml's own comment) that\nfallback does not actually happen: even after the previous commit set\ndestination.namespace and the Application CRs were re-applied, the\ncommitted hydrator.metadata + manifest.yaml on the environments/kind\nbranch still rendered Lakekeeper's db-migration Job with `namespace:\nargocd` (this Application's own metadata.namespace, not\ndestination.namespace). ArgoCD's sync hung forever waiting for that\nmisplaced hook Job's pod (CreateContainerConfigError -- it references\nSecrets that live in datalake-storage, not argocd) to complete.\n\nSetting sourceHydrator.drySource.helm.namespace explicitly on all three\ntier Applications bypasses the broken default and is what actually\nreaches the underlying `helm template --namespace` invocation.\ndestination.namespace stays set too -- it is what governs where\n`kubectl apply` targets any resource still lacking a namespace at sync\ntime, a real (if currently redundant, given helm.namespace) safety net.\n\nmake lint green.\n\n(per Task 4 in deliverables/plans/2026-08-06-datalake-v2-tenant-port-plan.md)\n"
}
